# IN-SCOPE: the six changed files are all named in the plan's Files, and the change is the mask-free open with the masks' program built afterwards, as step 18 describes, and nothing more.
# 
# Judged against this plan by its path and against the owner's messages as the scope check printed them. The substance of what was asked is that the editor become usable on the PC, where the build takes about 37 seconds; the diff addresses that and nothing else.
# 
# Files in the diff: NOTES.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, src/debug.ts, src/gl.ts (the picture-code module), src/main.ts, src/startup.ts. No untracked file, no version file, no decision record edit (option 11 is already in the record), no src/pipeline.ts change, no .contract-allow change.
# 
# Inside the plan, item by item:
# - The program built at open has the mask loops taken out (maskFreeFrag, dropMaskLoops, the masksAfter option that only the editor passes); the test page and the GPU export keep today's one program.
# - The masked program is built afterwards: started behind the picture where KHR_parallel_shader_compile is offered, with its completion read once per tick of the hold watch's existing timer (onWatchTick in startup.ts) and never waited on; built at the first draw of an edit holding a mask where it is not offered, after the busy card's words have painted, with busyWith set for the build and cleared after it.
# - A link that fails leaves the mask-free program in use and puts the driver's words in the report's Graphics build line.
# - Until the masked program is in use the edit is drawn as if it held no masks, by a copy of the parameters, so the masks on the edit are untouched; the coverage overlay is off for the same reason, which is a consequence of the same sentence and not an addition.
# - The test page's source imports the one shared function in place of its own copy; the pattern and the replacement text are identical, so its rows and output do not change. The Asked section says the test page is not touched, and Files and step 18 name src/debug.ts for exactly this reuse, so this is read as the plan's own instruction.
# - The Start-up line gains a masks clause and the frame watch counts the masks' build as a build; both exist so that the owner's one run on the PC can read what the build now costs, which the plan names as the run only the owner can make.
# - NOTES.md gains the new entry at the top of the staging section, with the PC numbers, the off-page and first-use split, the two vector-indexing lines as the next candidate, the test page's three rows and the cause, and the one run for the owner; the 071 bullet gains one line. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md changes only its generated line counts.
# 
# Not in the diff, and correctly: the iPad's sky wait, the look, the Aerochrome cap, the hub's gates, the camera JPEG, promotion, any walk or sheet, any change to a test-page row. This step judges scope only; the build, the checks and the pixel comparison are step 18's.
# 
# Found, not fixed: where the browser offers no parallel compile, a photograph that opens already holding saved masks starts the on-page build at its first draw, so the long build is paid then, after the card's words have painted. The plan accepts the on-page build at the first use of a mask. The PC run on a photograph holding no mask will show no masks build in the Start-up line until a mask is set.
